# The shared Berry interpreter's entry table (spec R7c.1, Phase 7c part 3,
# issue #431; tools/mkshlibc.py, ld/shberry.ld, <minix/shlibc.h>).
#
# One function per line; the line number (from 0, comments and blank lines
# not counted) is its slot in the table at the start of the library in
# flash (SHBERRY_BASE).  FROZEN like furi.exports: never reorder, insert
# or remove a name while GZ_ABI stays the same; new functions go at the END.
#
# Started 2026-11-21 with the functions the launcher (gzberry.c) calls,
# sorted by name.  (be_heap_limit, a variable, has no slot: it is
# PROVIDEd at its place in the berry area.)
be_data_push
be_dumpexcept
be_loadbuffer
be_loadmode
be_newobject
be_pcall
be_pop
be_pushstring
be_raise
be_repl
be_set_obs_hook
be_setglobal
be_toindex
be_tostring
be_vm_delete
be_vm_new
